<title>SOUTH AFRICA: S.African Q2 GDP rose annualised 3.5 pct.</title>
<headline>S.African Q2 GDP rose annualised 3.5 pct.</headline>
<dateline>PRETORIA 1996-08-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>South African gross domestic product (GDP) rose a seasonally adjusted and annualised 3.5 percent in the second quarter of 1996, the Central Statistical Service said.</p>
<p>It said first quarter GDP rose a revised 3.3 percent, unchanged from a preliminary 3.3 percent estimated rise.</p>
<p>The figures are at constant 1990 market prices.</p>
<p>A Reuters poll of economists forecast a second quarter rise of 4.2 percent.  </p>
<p>Seasonally adjusted and annualised percentage change:</p>
<p>    At market prices:    Q2'96 (prel)   Q1'96 (rev)   Q4'95</p>
<p>     GDP		     3.5		3.3	     2.7</p>
<p>At factor incomes:</p>
<p>     Total		   3.5		3.1	     1.7</p>
<p>     Agriculture	  41.2	     80.1	    -2.3</p>
<p>     Non-Agricultural    1.8		0.4	     1.9</p>
<p>     Mining		 -1.0		0.6	     2.5</p>
<p>     Secondary industry  1.7		0.3	    -1.6</p>
<p>     Manufacturing	 1.2	     -0.7	    -2.8</p>
<p>     Tertiary industry   2.4		0.5	     4.0</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom, +27 11 482-1003</p>
